{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778614277287,"sessionID":"ses_1e253fe4cffeINwag3mz2x0wkT","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"functions.read:0","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/home/runner/work/eval-ont-agent-mondo/eval-ont-agent-mondo/__issue_context__.json"},"output":"<path>/home/runner/work/eval-ont-agent-mondo/eval-ont-agent-mondo/__issue_context__.json</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: {\n2:   \"body\": \"**Preferred gene-related syndrome label**\\nFor example: NAA10-related syndrome\\nKY-related neuromyopathy\\n\\n**Synonyms**\\n\\n**Parent term (use [OLS](https://www.ebi.ac.uk/ols/ontologies/mondo), or your favorite ontology browser)**\\nMONDO:0100546 \\\"hereditary neuromuscular disease\\\"\\n\\n**Definition**\\nPlease write the definition in the format: Any [parent class] in which the cause of the disease is a mutation in the [gene name] gene. For example: Any congenital myopathy in which the cause of the disease is a mutation in the TPM3 gene.\\nAny neuromyopathy in which the cause of the disease is mutation in the KY gene. \\n\\n**Definition source (Please give PubMed ID, if applicable, in format PMID:#######)\\nThe ClinGen Muscular Dystrophy and Myopathy GCEP considers the below suggested children terms to be part of a spectrum of KY-related neuromyopathy. The group is still evaluating whether the myopathy associated with this gene should be considered myofibrillar myopathy, and so additional requests related to MONDO:0014922 \\\"myofibrillar myopathy 7\\\" may be made in the future.\\nPMID:27484770, PMID:27485408, PMID:28488683, PMID:32818658\\n\\n**Children terms (if applicable)** Should any existing terms be re-classified as children underneath this new proposed term? \\nMONDO:0014922 \\\"myofibrillar myopathy 7\\\"\\nMONDO:0044648 \\\"kyphoscoliosis-lateral tongue atrophy-hereditary spastic paraplegia syndrome\\\"\\nMONDO:0044647 \\\"kyphosis-lateral tongue atrophy-myofibrillar myopathy syndrome\\\"\\n \\n**Your nano-attribution (ORCID) or URL for a working group**\\nIf you don't have an ORCID, you can sign up for one [here](https://orcid.org/)\\nhttps://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40151/\\n0000-0002-2078-7280\",\n3:   \"comments\": [\n4:     {\n5:       \"id\": \"IC_kwDOBjach874slyD\",\n6:       \"author\": {\n7:         \"login\": \"katiermullen\"\n8:       },\n9:       \"authorAssociation\": \"MEMBER\",\n10:       \"body\": \"@clauseMDM thank you for this request. The new term, KY-related neuromyopathy, will be available in Mondo at the next release.\\n\\nThe three terms that you indicate will appear as children of this term. \\n\\nMONDO:0014922 \\\"myofibrillar myopathy 7\\\"\\nMONDO:0044648 \\\"kyphoscoliosis-lateral tongue atrophy-hereditary spastic paraplegia syndrome\\\"\\nMONDO:0044647 \\\"kyphosis-lateral tongue atrophy-myofibrillar myopathy syndrome\\\"\\n\\nPlease let us know if these need to be updated in the future.\\n\",\n11:       \"createdAt\": \"2026-04-01T19:21:07Z\",\n12:       \"includesCreatedEdit\": false,\n13:       \"isMinimized\": false,\n14:       \"minimizedReason\": \"\",\n15:       \"reactionGroups\": [],\n16:       \"url\": \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/9937#issuecomment-4172438659\",\n17:       \"viewerDidAuthor\": false\n18:     }\n19:   ],\n20:   \"title\": \"NTR/KY\",\n21:   \"url\": \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/9937\"\n22: }\n\n(End of file - total 22 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"{\n  \"body\": \"**Preferred gene-related syndrome label**\\nFor example: NAA10-related syndrome\\nKY-related neuromyopathy\\n\\n**Synonyms**\\n\\n**Parent term (use [OLS](https://www.ebi.ac.uk/ols/ontologies/mondo), or your favorite ontology browser)**\\nMONDO:0100546 \\\"hereditary neuromuscular disease\\\"\\n\\n**Definition**\\nPlease write the definition in the format: Any [parent class] in which the cause of the disease is a mutation in the [gene name] gene. For example: Any congenital myopathy in which the cause of the disease is a mutation in the TPM3 gene.\\nAny neuromyopathy in which the cause of the disease is mutation in the KY gene. \\n\\n**Definition source (Please give PubMed ID, if applicable, in format PMID:#######)\\nThe ClinGen Muscular Dystrophy and Myopathy GCEP considers the below suggested children terms to be part of a spectrum of KY-related neuromyopathy. The group is still evaluating whether the myopathy associated with this gene should be considered myofibrillar myopathy, and so additional requests related to MONDO:0014922 \\\"myofibrillar myopathy 7\\\" may be made in the future.\\nPMID:27484770, PMID:27485408, PMID:28488683, PMID:32818658\\n\\n**Children terms (if applicable)** Should any existing terms be re-classified as children underneath this new proposed term? \\nMONDO:0014922 \\\"myofibrillar myopathy 7\\\"\\nMONDO:0044648 \\\"kyphoscoliosis-lateral tongue atrophy-hereditary spastic paraplegia syndrome\\\"\\nMONDO:0044647 \\\"kyphosis-lateral tongue atrophy-myofibrillar myopathy syndrome\\\"\\n \\n**Your nano-attribution (ORCID) or URL for a working group**\\nIf you don't have an ORCID, you can sign up for one [here](https://orcid.org/)\\nhttps://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40151/\\n0000-0002-2078-7280\",\n  \"comments\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"IC_kwDOBjach874slyD\",\n      \"author\": {\n        \"login\": \"katiermullen\"\n      },\n      \"authorAssociation\": \"MEMBER\",\n      \"body\": \"@clauseMDM thank you for this request. The new term, KY-related neuromyopathy, will be available in Mondo at the next release.\\n\\nThe three terms that you indicate will appear as children of this term. \\n\\nMONDO:0014922 \\\"myofibrillar myopathy 7\\\"\\nMONDO:0044648 \\\"kyphoscoliosis-lateral tongue atrophy-hereditary spastic paraplegia syndrome\\\"\\nMONDO:0044647 \\\"kyphosis-lateral tongue atrophy-myofibrillar myopathy syndrome\\\"\\n\\nPlease let us know if these need to be updated in the future.\\n\",\n      \"createdAt\": 